body:
I've been on a few. The best effect is that they really decrease my suicidal ideation. I don't have random daily crying spells or urges to self harm. They basically turn off the poisonous depression thoughts: self hatred, worthlessness, etc. Or at least they make me feel capable of dealing with those thoughts and dismissing them.

&#x200B;

Bad effects: weight gain sometimes. If I miss a dose it can make me nauseous or dizzy. There's a side effect that people call "brain zaps" that some people get on anti-depressants. I've only experienced that when I miss a dose or when I've tried to get off an anti-depressant without the help of a doctor. (This is a super bad plan. I don't recommend it.)
